astrobench_a877243f10,astrobench_a877243f10_chunk_033,33,"must be cancelled by the other two terms in the bracket. That is, as vφ→0 at least one of∂Jr/∂vφand∂Jz/∂vφmust tend to a non-zero value that after weighting by the frequencies magically cancels t he last term.(Piﬄ et al. 2015). Piﬄ et al. (2015) pointed out that taking the argumentoffto be a linear combination Jof the actions as proposed by B14 prevents the three terms in the big bracket of equa- tion (5) cancelling, and thus causes ∂f/∂v φ/negationslash= 0 atvφ= 0, which conﬂicts with both physical intuition and Gaia data. The DF needs to be structured such that the three terms do cancel in the limit vφ→0. Satisfaction of the condition lim vφ→0∂f ∂vφ= 0 (6) actually achieves two things. In addition to ensuring that a t any location the distribution in vφdoesn’t have a cusp or dimple at vφ= 0, it ensures that the distribution of velocity components vxandvyparallel to the equatorial plane tends smoothly to isotropy as the symmetry axis is approached – this behaviour is imperative because on the axis all direc- tions perpendicular to the axis",3 ANALYTIC CONSIDERATIONS,3 ANALYTIC CONSIDERATIONS,,,,,Distribution functions for spheroids,James Binney,astro-ph.GA,2026-02-26T15:41:51Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23127v1,2602.23127,distribution_functions,234,180,False,True,140,320,False,2.5
