astrobench_3474c47fe1,astrobench_3474c47fe1_chunk_034,34,"of the truncation and transforms to a purely Keplerian de- cline for𝑟≳𝑟 T. All quantities in the top row are, at fixed radius, monotonically increasing functions of𝑟 Tand𝜉. The panels on the bottom row of Fig. 2 show, from left to right, the relative potential, the surface density profile, and the cumula- tive projected mass profile. As for the quantities shown in the top row, at fixed (projected) radius, all of these quantities are increasing functions of𝑟 Tand𝜉. A difference is that the truncation affects the quantitiesshowninthebottomrowatevery(projected)radius,even at(projected)radiismallerthan𝜉𝑟 T.Indeed,eachofthesequantities depends on the density at all radii, including those at large radii. For example, the potential is not only affected at large radii, with a Keplerian decline beyond the truncation radius, but the depth of the potential well,Ψ 0, is also reduced by the truncation.",3.2 Basic properties,3.2 Basic properties,,,,,Self-consistent dynamical models with a finite extent -- V. Smooth radial truncations and phase-space consistency,Maarten Baes,astro-ph.GA,2026-01-13T09:17:21Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.08361v1,2601.08361,distribution_functions,175,134,False,False,140,274,False,2.0
astrobench_3474c47fe1,astrobench_3474c47fe1_chunk_035,35,"would not in- validate the models as instantaneous equilibria, but it would imply that they represent metastable configurations whose long-term evo- lution may involve slow reorganisation of the central structure. Thesituationbecomesricherforanisotropicdistributionfunctions. Strongradialanisotropyisknowntotriggertheradial-orbitinstability (Antonov1973;Hénon1973;Polyachenko&Shukhman1981,2015; Merritt & Aguilar 1985; Barnes et al. 1986), and numerous studies have quantified stability limits for Osipkov–Merritt models in terms oftheanisotropyradiusorglobalanisotropyparameters(e.g.Palmer & Papaloizou 1987; Saha 1991; Nipoti et al. 2002; Di Cintio & Casetti 2020). In addition, anisotropic spherical systems generically supportweaklydampedglobalmodes(Weinberg1991,1994;Heggie et al. 2020), which can be destabilised by relatively small features",4.3 Stability considerations,4.3 Stability considerations,,,,,Self-consistent dynamical models with a finite extent -- V. Smooth radial truncations and phase-space consistency,Maarten Baes,astro-ph.GA,2026-01-13T09:17:21Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.08361v1,2601.08361,distribution_functions,112,86,False,False,280,366,False,2.0
