astrobench_15ca427d22,astrobench_15ca427d22_chunk_007,7,"accurately fit the Cepheid tracers, prompting us to select stars within the young stars’ age range in the simulation for comparison with the Cepheid data. As Chen et al. (2019) note, the parameters ofa,bandR wshow a clear correlation, whereasϕ wis a more independent parameter in the geometric warp model. Consequently, while different studies might yield varying a,bandR wvalues,ϕ wtends to be more consistent across measurements of the Galactic warp. Figure 4 illustrates the time evolution of the warp amplitude in the stellar and gas disks. The amplitude is calculated by fitting Eq. 7 to the warp every 0.01 Gyr starting fromt= 3 Gyr—after the merger is completed—and identifying the maximum amplitude atR= 16 kpc, which is near the simulated disk edge. The warp is measured using young disk particles selected based on circularityϵ=L Z/LZ,max(E) >0.65 and age less than 1.5 Gyr in the simulation. This selection reflects that the warp is most prominent among the youngest stars and spans multiple age populations (Chen et al. 2019; Cheng et al. 2020; Huang et al. 2024). The dashed lines in both panels",4.GALACTIC VERTICAL WAVES,4.GALACTIC VERTICAL WAVES,,,,,A Low-mass Model of The Milky Way: The Disk Warp Resulting from A Galaxy Merger,"Mingji Deng, Cuihua Du, Jian Zhang, Haoyang Liu, Zhongbcheng Li",astro-ph.GA,2026-01-29T12:41:33Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.21638v1,2601.21638,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,True,280,460,False,3.0
astrobench_15ca427d22,astrobench_15ca427d22_chunk_008,8,"Gyr in the simulation. This selection reflects that the warp is most prominent among the youngest stars and spans multiple age populations (Chen et al. 2019; Cheng et al. 2020; Huang et al. 2024). The dashed lines in both panels represent the observed amplitudes of the Milky Way’s stellar and gas disk warps (Chen et al. 2019; Levine et al. 2006). We specifically focus on this young population for three reasons. First, older stellar populations (e.g.,≤4 Gyr) exhibit significant vertical dispersion, which introduces noise into the warp signal (Deng et al. 2024; Han et al. 2023). Second, observational studies indicate that warp kinematics derived from young tracers, such as Cepheids (∼100 Myr), show consistent constraints on the precession rate and LoN orientation, whereas results from older tracers remain inconclusive (see Figure 8 in Cabrera-Gadea et al. 2024). Finally, we tested the robustness of our selection by comparing it with a broader sample including stars up to 4 Gyr. We found that in the early stage, when the proportion of old stars is high, the measurements will deviate from those of",4.GALACTIC VERTICAL WAVES,4.GALACTIC VERTICAL WAVES,,,,,A Low-mass Model of The Milky Way: The Disk Warp Resulting from A Galaxy Merger,"Mingji Deng, Cuihua Du, Jian Zhang, Haoyang Liu, Zhongbcheng Li",astro-ph.GA,2026-01-29T12:41:33Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.21638v1,2601.21638,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,False,420,600,False,3.0
